at might actually be good at showdown. Folding throws away equity when I might have the best hand.\n\nReason: My opponent has shown extreme weakness by checking through all four betting rounds. While my 10-high (or Ace-high using the board) is terrible, their passive play suggests they likely have nothing either - possibly not even a pair. Checking costs me nothing and gives me a chance to win at showdown with my Ace-high. The pot is small, so bluffing risks too much for minimal reward. I should check and see if my hand is good.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
